      "reply": "```python\nVIDEO_W, VIDEO_H = 1920, 1080\nCROP_W, CROP_H = 1440, 1080\nSCALE = 2\n\nCROP_X0 = (VIDEO_W - CROP_W) / 2  # 240\nCROP_Y0 = (VIDEO_H - CROP_H) / 2  # 0\n\n\ndef to_tracker(x, y):\n    \"\"\"Convert a pixel position in the original 1920x1080 video to tracker\n    coordinates (center crop 1440x1080, downscaled by 2 -> 720x540).\n\n    Returns (x, y) as floats, or None if the point lies outside the crop.\n    \"\"\"\n    cx = x - CROP_X0\n    cy = y - CROP_Y0\n    if not (0 <= cx < CROP_W and 0 <= cy < CROP_H):\n        return None\n    return (cx / SCALE, cy / SCALE)\n```",
